#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:0
msgid ""
"Share your desktop over RDP with Desktop Sharing or Remote Login, find the "
"connection details and open the firewall ports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:8
msgid "Topics: Remote access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:12
msgid "Share your desktop remotely"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:14
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"Related test plan: <https://wiki.ubuntu.com/DesktopTeam/TestPlans/"
"RemoteDesktop>\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:18
msgid ""
"You can enable remote desktop sharing on your system. This way, you or other "
"people will be able to view or control your desktop from another computer in "
"real time. The desktop sharing works over the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:20
msgid ""
"We'll refer to the system that shares its desktop as the *server*. We'll "
"call the system that accesses the shared desktop remotely the *client*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:22
msgid "What you'll need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:25
msgid "Ubuntu Desktop 24.04 LTS or later with GNOME on the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:26
msgid ""
"If you want to share your desktop outside of your local network, you need "
"access to your router's configuration, the ability to configure a Virtual "
"Private Network (VPN) or reach out to your network administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:28
msgid "Allow another person to view your screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:30
msgid ""
"With the **Desktop Sharing** feature, another person using a different "
"computer can view your screen while you're using your computer. Optionally, "
"you can allow the other person to control your environment. You must be "
"logged in before the other person can connect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:32
msgid ""
"The resolution of the shared screen is determined by your user session on "
"the server. Therefore, the screen might look **too small, too large or "
"blurry** due to scaling on the client."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:34
msgid ""
"To allow this access, go to {menuselection}`Settings --> System --> Remote "
"Desktop --> Desktop Sharing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:36
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"The reason for this screenshot is that the host name, user name and password "
"might be confusing to the reader or too abstract if not seen in context of "
"the remote desktop configuration.\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:39
msgid ""
"![Desktop Sharing enabled in Settings](/images/gnome-remote-desktop.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:39
msgid "Desktop Sharing enabled in Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:41
msgid "Allow logging into your account from another computer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:43
msgid ""
"With the **Remote Login** feature, you or another person can log into your "
"account from another, remote computer. You must be logged out before the "
"remote user can connect. If you are already logged in at the time, they get "
"the option to terminate your running session and log in remotely instead. "
"The connecting user has full control over your environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:45
msgid ""
"The resolution of the shared screen is determined by the window on the "
"client. Therefore, the screen is always the **right size and looks sharp**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:47
msgid ""
"To allow this access, go to {menuselection}`Settings --> System --> Remote "
"Desktop --> Remote Login`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:49
msgid "Find the access credentials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:51
msgid ""
"When you connect from a remote client, you have to know the remote desktop "
"user name and password, the host name of the server and the port number that "
"provides RDP access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:53
msgid "User name and password"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:55
msgid ""
"In {menuselection}`Settings --> System --> Remote Desktop`, note down the "
"user name and password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:57
msgid ""
"These are different from your regular user credentials, and they only work "
"for the remote desktop sharing. You can change them here without affecting "
"how you log in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:59
msgid "Host name on the local network"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:61
msgid ""
"To point the client to the location of your server, you need either the "
"server host name or its IP address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:63
msgid ""
"If the server and client are both on the **same network**, for example on "
"**your home Wi-Fi**, you can use the host name that you find in "
"{menuselection}`Settings --> System --> Remote Desktop`. You might need to "
"add the `.local` suffix at the end when entering it on the client."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:65
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can use the IPv4 address of the server. Display your "
"local IPv4 address:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:0
msgid "Graphical interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:72
msgid ""
"If you're using wired network, go to {menuselection}`Settings --> Wired --> "
"your connected network --> Network Options (gear icon) --> IPv4 Address`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:74
msgid ""
"If you're on Wi-Fi, go to {menuselection}`Settings --> Wi-Fi --> your "
"connected network --> Network Options (gear icon) --> IPv4 Address`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:0
msgid "Command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:-1
msgid ""
"[...]\n"
"2: wlp0s20f3: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> [...]\n"
"    inet 192.168.0.91/24 [...]\n"
"[...]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:93
msgid "Here, your IPv4 address is 192.168.0.91."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:97
msgid ""
"The local IPv4 address might change when you reboot the server or reconnect "
"to the network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:100
msgid "Host name on a public network"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:102
msgid ""
"If you're sharing the desktop between **different networks**, for example "
"between **your office and your home Wi-Fi**, you need a public IPv4 or IPv6 "
"address for the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:104
msgid ""
"You might have to configure port forwarding in your router's configuration, "
"or set up access to the server through a VPN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:107
msgid ""
"With port forwarding, you open up your system to the world. This is a "
"security risk because attackers might try to break into your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:109
msgid ""
"If you only want to share the desktop with a private group of people, use "
"the VPN instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:112
msgid "Check with your internet provider or your network administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:114
msgid "Port number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:116
msgid ""
"By default, Desktop Sharing and Remote Login both use the 3389 port on your "
"system. However, if you enable them both at the same time, Desktop Sharing "
"switches to port 3390, while Remote Login keeps port 3389. You can then "
"choose the connection type to use at the remote client by setting the port "
"number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:118
msgid "Open RDP ports in your firewall"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:120
msgid "If the firewall is active, allow RDP connections to your system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:127
msgid ""
"If the Firewall (`gufw`) application is installed, open it and go to the "
"Rules tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:129
msgid ""
"Click {guilabel}`Add a rule…` ({guilabel}`+`). Switch to the Simple tab. "
"Enter the following configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:131
msgid "**Policy:** Allow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:133
msgid "**Direction:** In"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:135
msgid "**Protocol:** TCP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:137
msgid "**Port:** 3389:3390"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:139
msgid "Click {guilabel}`Add` to confirm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:161
msgid "Connect from a client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:163
msgid ""
"To connect to this system from a remote client, use an application that "
"supports RDP. Enter the credentials that you've noted down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/share-your-desktop-remotely.md:165
msgid ""
"On Ubuntu, you can use the Remmina application. See {ref}`access-a-remote-"
"desktop`."
msgstr ""
